**Read:** [DC Electrical Circuit Analysis — James M. Fiore](../sources/DC-Electrical-Circuit-Analysis-Fiore.lingua#r_4A9FXBXKNPS4JV50QQ3TVPS2GV), complete introductory quantities, components and network chapters; [Sistemas elétricos de potência — Arlei Bichels](../sources/Sistemas-Eletricos-de-Potencia-Bichels.lingua#r_5T4SVBJ6FAPQWJPVNQV4Y6427G), introductory system/component representations.

A voltage is a potential difference or defined terminal measurement between points; current is a signed flow of charge through a selected boundary. A port pairs voltage with an oriented current. A circuit node is an idealized equipotential connection within a chosen model; an actual extended busbar or earth structure can have spatial voltage differences.

Distinguish generator, converter, transformer, motor, feeder, bus, switch, disconnector, breaker, fuse, relay, sensor and controller by function. A relay decides or signals; a breaker interrupts current within its ratings. An isolating device is not automatically suitable for interrupting fault current. A transformer changes AC terminal relationships while conserving power only in an ideal lossless model; it is not a source of net energy.

Keep Portuguese equivalents alongside meaning: tensão, corrente, potência ativa/reativa/aparente, barramento, alimentador, disjuntor, seccionador, relé, neutro and condutor de proteção. Neutral, protective conductor and an abstract zero-volt reference have distinct roles. Draw a counterexample to each tempting equivalence. The later installation and fault studies replace ideal labels with explicit physical ratings, paths and operating evidence.

